{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Li2013-PSbPMMA-169nm",
  "Source": "X. Li, X. Yu, and Y. Han, \"Polymer thin films for antireflection coatings,\" J. Mater. Chem. C 1, 2266-2285 (2013). doi:10.1039/c2tc00529h - Text p. 2271 (Sec. 3.1, Eq. 8) and Fig. 6 caption, from ref. 17",
  "Notes": "Single-layer nanoporous PS-b-PMMA antireflection film (n = 1.23) on glass, middle thickness (Fig. 6b curve 2)\nSpecification: Zero reflectance at one wavelength: quarter-wave layer with n ~ 1.23.\nReported: Text p. 2271: minimum reflectance less than ~0.1 % (Fig. 6b). From Fig. 6b (plot only): minimum of curve (2) near 800-850 nm; quarter-wave condition gives 4 n d = 831 nm.\nNotes: Same assumptions as Li2013-PSbPMMA-126nm (n = 1.23 film, glass n = 1.52 semi-infinite, normal incidence, no dispersion). reference_nm = 4 n d, not stated in the paper.\nLayers from Text p. 2271 (Sec. 3.1, Eq. 8) and Fig. 6 caption, from ref. 17; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R min 0.001 % at 831 nm; paper R min < ~0.1 %; 4nd = 831 nm.",
